# Environment variables the janux server ACTUALLY reads (G-134).
#
# This file is documentation, not configuration: there is no dotenv
# dependency and nothing loads `.env` automatically. Export these in
# your shell, systemd unit, or compose `environment:` block if you need
# them. Everything else lives in the layered TOML files (base.toml +
# seed.toml, see README "Configuration").
#
# ── Config file selection ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path to the config file(s); defaults to the `base` + `seed` pair.
# Same as `janux -c <path>`.
#JANUX_CONFIG_FILE=/etc/janux/janux.toml

# Selects an optional `config/{RUN_ENV}.toml` overlay (defaults to
# "development"; the overlay is skipped when the file does not exist).
#RUN_ENV=production

# ── Field overrides ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any JanuxConfig field can be overridden with the JANUX__ prefix and
# __ separator (config crate Environment source — highest precedence,
# above every file). Examples:
#JANUX__ENCRYPTION_KEY=<64 hex chars — REQUIRED; base.toml's encryption_key>
#JANUX__DATA_DIR=/var/lib/janux
#JANUX__TRUST_FORWARDED_HEADERS=false

# ── NOT environment variables ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Provider credentials are per-tenant SEED config, not env:
#   mail (magic links)   → [seed.resend]   in seed.toml
#   SMS (Aliyun)         → [seed.alisms]   in seed.toml
#   social OAuth         → [[seed.providers]] in seed.toml
# Signing keys, OAuth2 clients and policies are data — created via the
# admin API or seed.toml, never via env.
